# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The rule here is NOT "is it generated?" — it is "what does it cost a
# teammate to regenerate?"
#
# The pipeline's outputs are generated, but regenerating them means an OCR
# pass, a vision model captioning every figure, and hundreds of LLM calls
# against a model they may not even have pulled. Those are committed, so a
# clone is a working library on first run.
#
# Machine-local state (paths, concurrency, caches keyed to this machine) is
# ignored, because sharing it actively breaks the next person's setup.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Python ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# ── Machine-local settings ──
# Concurrency and context windows tuned to THIS machine's hardware; sharing
# them would hand a laptop a workstation's settings.
/config/runtime.json
# Where this machine keeps its source PDFs.
/.betteringest.json
# Exact-key replay of local runs — a debugging aid, not a shared artifact.
/.debug_cache/
# Evaluation output: raw payloads and derived records of measured runs.
# Large, machine-specific, and regenerated by the scripts under evaluation/.
/evaluation/results/

# ── Ingest working directory ──
# Page renders and intermediate crops. The finished copies live in
# knowledge_base/assets/ (which IS committed), so this is a duplicate that
# grows with every PDF.
/.betteringest_out/*
!/.betteringest_out/captions.json

# ── Rust / Tauri build output ──
tauri-app/src-tauri/target/
tauri-app/src-tauri/gen/*

# ── Frontend / package manager output ──
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.vite/

# ── Test and type-check caches ──
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/

# ── macOS ──
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble

# ── Editor ──
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ── Claude Code ──
# Project settings are shared; per-user overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DELIBERATELY COMMITTED — do not add these back
#
#   knowledge_base/        Ingested markdown, figure assets and the manifest.
#                          Behind these: OCR, layout reconstruction and a
#                          vision model captioning every table and figure.
#   index/                 The document trees, including LLM summaries.
#   index/.facets/         Pre-filter judgements — one LLM call per passage
#                          per question. 268 calls for this corpus alone, and
#                          they are keyed by content hash, so a clone reuses
#                          every one of them instead of paying again.
#   .ocr_cache/            OCR layouts keyed by file hash. Portable by
#                          construction, and the single most expensive step
#                          to repeat.
#   .betteringest_out/captions.json
#                          Vision-model captions, also hash-keyed.
#   tauri-app/src-tauri/Cargo.lock
#                          This is an application, not a library: the lock
#                          file is what makes a teammate's build reproducible.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Golden eval labels: which page answers which question. Derived data —
# regenerate with `python3 evaluation/golden_from_csv.py <questions.csv>`.
# Committing it would publish exactly which pages a question set sampled.
knowledge_base/.golden.json

# MinerU ingest working area and its source-folder setting. Crops are
# regenerable from the PDF in seconds; captions.json is 20 minutes of vision
# model per document and is hash-keyed, so it is kept — the same split as
# .betteringest_out/.
/.mineru_out/*
!/.mineru_out/captions.json
/.mineru.json
